<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16259" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">essĕdārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		essedum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
				war-chariot</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 45, 7</span></i>
			.—Hence, as <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">essedari-us</span></b> , i,
				m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A fighter in a</i> (Gallic or British) <i>war-chariot</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				4, 24, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 15, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 19, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fam. 7, 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In the Roman circus, <i>a gladiator</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 36, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Calig. 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Claud. 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 2566</span></i>; v. essedum.</div>
